// Field reference: https://github.com/peterellisjones/dronecom-community/blob/main/data/docs/components.md
//
// Air-class RWR spoofer (#5172). Radiates a fake search-radar fingerprint at
// 45 MW — enough to be believed as one of the mid-ladder airborne search sets,
// and objectively too weak to be believed as an AN/SPY-310. A spoofer's claim
// is checked against its real radiated power by any ESM-class (FDOA-capable)
// receiver: `|20*log10(emission_strength / claimed)| > spoof_power_tolerance_db`
// (12 dB, i.e. a power ratio of x/ 3.98) and the claim is rejected in favour of
// this component's own id. Every entry in `emulates` below sits inside that band
// at 45 MW; an_aps_660 (200 MW) and an_spy_310 (300 MW) do not, which is why
// they are absent and why selling the big-array lie needs the AN/SLQ-80's
// generator instead. The pairing is pinned by the plausibility sweep in
// `dc_sim::ops::portrayed_signature`, so this list cannot drift out of band
// unnoticed.
//
// `emulates` is kept domain-coherent by authoring discipline, not by a sim
// rule: nothing ties a portrayed emitter's domain to the hull portraying it.
// Lead with airborne search sets, and include a surface set only where the
// class's power can honestly reach it (an_sps_90, the one a USV-80 carrying
// this payload would claim). Keep new entries coherent the same way.
//
// ORDER IS LIVE GAMEPLAY: the first entry is what this payload claims with no
// doctrine selection. an_aps_440 leads because a mid-ladder airborne search
// radar is the most useful default lie.
(
    id: "an_alq_50",
    designator: "AN/ALQ-50",
    codename: "Mockingbird",
    category: Decoys,
    mount_rule: Single,
    weight: 25.0,
    // Fits every air drone from the RQ-10 (2.5 kW headroom) upward with room
    // for a receiver. Decoy draw is authored, never derived: it is the epic's
    // class gate against `power_supply_kw`, not a function of capability.
    power_draw: Fixed(1.5),
    // Unrestricted on purpose. Which hulls may carry a deception payload is
    // the chassis's `Category(Decoys)` grant; which payload they can afford is
    // the weight and power budget. No domain fiat.
    allowed: [],
    payload: Decoy((
        channel: EmitterSpoofer(
            emulates: ["an_aps_440", "an_aps_150", "an_aps_320", "an_sps_90"],
            emission_strength: 45000000.0,
            mounting: Hull,
        ),
    )),
)
